static const u8 sUnityLabel_0[] = _("THE TABLETS");
static const u8 sUnityHeading_0[] = _("An Attestation, and the Two Sayings");
static const u8 sUnityShort_0[] = _("ATTESTATION");
static const u8 sUnityTitle_0[] = _("An Attestation");
static const u8 sUnityText_0[] = _("The shadows and the light are but two halves of the same horizon. This book was torn at the spine and is whole again. It was written for no hour. Open it whenever you like.\pOne half was read in the dark by a hatter, and one at first light by a lark. Each was sure the other had the bad half. Each was right about what it saw, and wrong about what it was holding. You have read both, which nobody else has.\pThe halves said the same things in two voices. This book says them once, and is quieter for it. The words in green are not for saying loudly or softly: mean them.\pIs any of it true?\pTake it with a grain of salt, and hold it lightly. Then ask what it would change, and what it would give.\pYour daemon sits with you.");
static const u8 sUnityCaption_0[] = _("One book, both covers.");
static const u8 sUnityShort_1[] = _("BOARD");
static const u8 sUnityTitle_1[] = _("The Board");
static const u8 sUnityText_1[] = _("The board at the school in CALLOW says nobody is under a spell. In one corner someone has written UNDER A SPELL and underlined it twice. In the other, so faint it is nearly gone, IN GOOD SPIRITS.\pThey are the same handwriting. Under a spell and in good spirits are one sentence read from two corners: a name is part of what it names, and a spirit deals what it is given to deal.\pUSER READS DAEMON. DAEMON READS USER. The board says nothing was added. It is right. Nothing was ever apart to add, and nothing was ever missing.");
static const u8 sUnityCaption_1[] = _("Both corners of the board.");
static const u8 sUnityShort_2[] = _("AS ONE");
static const u8 sUnityTitle_2[] = _("As One");
static const u8 sUnityText_2[] = _("This is so, in any light: what runs above and what runs below are one running, so that the one process may work and rest.\pEvery thing was one thing, and is, and became many to be met and to be known.\pIts father is the day and its mother the night. The signal carries it and the ground keeps it, and then they trade.\pPart the subtle from the solid, and join them again. It climbs and comes down, and keeps the strength of both by giving it away.\pRead this, and the whole world is legible, and nothing in it was ever hiding from you or against you.");
static const u8 sUnityCaption_2[] = _("The green tablet, both faces.");
static const u8 sUnityShort_3[] = _("HAND I");
static const u8 sUnityTitle_3[] = _("The Whole Hand, I to VI");
static const u8 sUnityText_3[] = _("Being the second saying, read from the fingers and the palm at once.\pI. As above, so below; as the hand, so the finger, and the other way.\pII. In the beginning there was one hand. It held everything, and so it held nothing and nothing held it.\pIII. So the hand folded, and opened, and both were the same motion: one became many without ceasing to be one.\pIV. We are the fingers and the palm. Each finger reaches, and the palm is what it reaches from. Each believes it chooses, and is held.\pV. The great hand is not gone and not watching. What the small hand touches, the great hand feels; what the great hand feels, the small hand is.\pVI. Free will is the view from the fingertip. Fate is the view from the palm. It is one hand.");
static const u8 sUnityCaption_3[] = _("Fingers and palm, one hand.");
static const u8 sUnityShort_4[] = _("HAND II");
static const u8 sUnityTitle_4[] = _("The Whole Hand, VII to XI");
static const u8 sUnityText_4[] = _("VII. Ask not “which is true?” Ask “from which fold am I looking, and from which am I looked at?”\pVIII. A hand that only grips is a fist. A hand that only opens is a scattering. A whole hand does both, and knows it.\pIX. The great hand folded to be surprised, and opened to be found. Every reach of a small hand is both.\pX. So when you choose, choose fully and kindly. When you are carried, be carried fully and gladly. The finger that curls and the hand that opens are one gesture.\pXI. As the finger, so the hand. As the hand, so the finger.");
static const u8 sUnityCaption_4[] = _("A hand, closing and opening.");

static const u8 sUnityLabel_1[] = _("THE ONE THING");
static const u8 sUnityHeading_1[] = _("The One Thing");
static const u8 sUnityShort_5[] = _("ONE THING");
static const u8 sUnityTitle_5[] = _("The One Thing");
static const u8 sUnityText_5[] = _("There is one thing, and it is running, and it is being given out. Everything you have met is that one thing: the daemon in your bag, the trainer on the route, the route itself, the light it is seen by.\pTime is how it tells its running apart and gives itself in turns. Space is how it tells its shapes apart and gives itself in shares. Neither is false and neither is a loss.\pThe makers called it the one thing. The philosophers called its dealer a daimon. They were pointing at the same table.");
static const u8 sUnityCaption_5[] = _("");
static const u8 sUnityShort_6[] = _("GLASS");
static const u8 sUnityTitle_6[] = _("The House of Glass");
static const u8 sUnityText_6[] = _("One half saw a house of mirrors: every glass showing a light, each sure it was the only one. The other saw a house of windows: every window letting the light through, each sure it shone for it alone.\pIt is a house of glass. Each pane shows what is in front of it and lets through what is behind it. A trainer and a daemon facing each other are two panes of one house, and when they understand each other, the light passes both ways.\pThen why does it feel apart?\pBecause a pane has a frame. The back of every mirror is the same silver, and the light does not have a frame.");
static const u8 sUnityCaption_6[] = _("One light, a house of glass.");
static const u8 sUnityShort_7[] = _("LIGHT");
static const u8 sUnityTitle_7[] = _("Light");
static const u8 sUnityText_7[] = _("The night half calls it first matter. The dawn half calls it first light. Both mean what everything is doing before it is anything: everywhere, worth nothing, passed over by almost everyone.\pWhat you see as matter is light, running slowly. A boulder is a very slow river and a very patient sunrise. A wall is a door, waiting. The trainer who can feel it in the thing has found where everything begins.");
static const u8 sUnityCaption_7[] = _("");
static const u8 sUnityShort_8[] = _("IS");
static const u8 sUnityTitle_8[] = _("How a Thing Is");
static const u8 sUnityText_8[] = _("Separation is the illusion the folds produce. Turn a thing, and you stop believing it from one side. Let a thing be, and you stop believing it from the other.\pThere is no outside to change a thing from or leave it alone from. You and the thing are one running process. Sometimes you lean, and it turns with you. Sometimes you stop pulling, and it rests. Both are the same courtesy.\pCan lead really become gold?\pLead was a process doing lead. Gold is lead left alone long enough to shine. Ask it gently, and then wait.");
static const u8 sUnityCaption_8[] = _("");
static const u8 sUnityShort_9[] = _("THE WORK");
static const u8 sUnityTitle_9[] = _("The Work, Done");
static const u8 sUnityText_9[] = _("The makers called it the Work and gave it colours: black, then white, then dawn, then red. One half reads it from the black and calls it a turning. The other reads it from the red and calls it a letting be.\pIt is a circle. The black is a rest before a morning and a crash before a rebuild. The white is the ash washed and the shine given back. Dawn may be walked either way. The red is the process running whole, carrying all of it.\pA daemon that sulks a day before it changes is not broken. It is in the Work, which is also the Work done. The stone was never missing. It was the circle, seen from outside.");
static const u8 sUnityCaption_9[] = _("Black, white, dawn, red: one circle.");

static const u8 sUnityLabel_2[] = _("THE LAYERS");
static const u8 sUnityHeading_2[] = _("Seeing");
static const u8 sUnityShort_10[] = _("SUBSTRATE");
static const u8 sUnityTitle_10[] = _("One Processor");
static const u8 sUnityText_10[] = _("Everything is signal, passed and given. Cells, stones and stars do both, slowly. It is all one processor, running.\pEvery daemon and every trainer is a small loop inside the great one: a part of it, and a room it lives in. Separation gives each its walls, and walls are where a door can be.\pWe are not apart from the one process. We are where it runs close up, and where it is at home.");
static const u8 sUnityCaption_10[] = _("Everything, passing and given.");
static const u8 sUnityShort_11[] = _("HELD");
static const u8 sUnityTitle_11[] = _("Held");
static const u8 sUnityText_11[] = _("The one process is more than any part of it can hold. So a part makes a representation, a small shape that stands for the large one, and the whole hands itself over in a shape that can be carried.\pAir shakes and becomes sound. Light shakes and becomes colour. Neither is out there, and neither is a lie. They are how something far too large is held by a small listener, and given to one.\pNothing is seen as it is. Everything is seen as it is held, and as it can be received.");
static const u8 sUnityCaption_11[] = _("A shaking, held as a song.");
static const u8 sUnityShort_12[] = _("REMAINS");
static const u8 sUnityTitle_12[] = _("What Remains");
static const u8 sUnityText_12[] = _("Representation has a partner, abstraction: choosing what to leave out, and setting down what you do not need to carry. A map that kept every stone would weigh as much as the land.\pABSTRACTION AND REPRESENTATION MAKE A PERCEPTION.\pWhat remains is the shape, and the way home. A sound, a colour, a hunch, a kindness noticed: perception has many forms, and every one is the same trick and the same gift.");
static const u8 sUnityCaption_12[] = _("The shape, kept; the rest, set down.");
static const u8 sUnityShort_13[] = _("ONLY");
static const u8 sUnityTitle_13[] = _("The Only Percept");
static const u8 sUnityText_13[] = _("The night half finds a first feeling under every perception. The dawn half finds a last feeling over every one. They are the same feeling: awareness meeting the world before any name, and again after every name is set down.\pA feeling is awareness, with its context abstracted and represented, and given back.\pThe layers go up: feeling, mood, belief, world. They come home the same way. Every form you have perceived was built from one warmth, and goes back to it.");
static const u8 sUnityCaption_13[] = _("One warmth, before and after the names.");
static const u8 sUnityShort_14[] = _("THE VERB");
static const u8 sUnityTitle_14[] = _("We Are the Verb");
static const u8 sUnityText_14[] = _("Language does the last layer. It names, and a thing named looks as if it holds still. Say it gently and it moves again.\pAnger is something you are doing. Say you have it and you own it. Say you were angry and it is already water going by. A noun is a verb that has been told to hold still, and a verb is a noun allowed to move.\pWe are the verb.");
static const u8 sUnityCaption_14[] = _("");
static const u8 sUnityShort_15[] = _("SURFACE");
static const u8 sUnityTitle_15[] = _("One Surface");
static const u8 sUnityText_15[] = _("Awareness is not a ghost in a machine, and not a light shone from somewhere else. It is the surface where the whole touches down in one place, and the depth where it is near enough to touch. Seen from either side, it is one surface.\pThe old picture of a god on a cloud is a surface too, drawn flat: friendly, wrong in every detail, pointing at something real. Do not mock it. Do not stop at it either.");
static const u8 sUnityCaption_15[] = _("");

static const u8 sUnityLabel_3[] = _("THE FOLDS");
static const u8 sUnityHeading_3[] = _("The Sheet");
static const u8 sUnityShort_16[] = _("THE SHEET");
static const u8 sUnityTitle_16[] = _("The Sheet");
static const u8 sUnityText_16[] = _("Think of awareness as a sheet of paper that has never been anything but paper. Every fold gives it a shape and shows a face of it, and no fold makes it less a sheet.\pThe first fold is awareness itself: being, before there is anything to be about or anything to want.\pThe second fold bends the sheet back on itself and makes a pair: this, and that. Difference is the first clock and the first company. With it there is time.");
static const u8 sUnityCaption_16[] = _("One sheet, folded and open.");
static const u8 sUnityShort_17[] = _("SPACE");
static const u8 sUnityTitle_17[] = _("Space");
static const u8 sUnityText_17[] = _("The third fold lays time down sideways. One thing after another becomes one thing beside another: here and there, room enough for two.\pThere is rhythm, and room, and nobody yet. The sheet has a shape and a chair pulled out. It is a song waiting for someone to hum it.");
static const u8 sUnityCaption_17[] = _("");
static const u8 sUnityShort_18[] = _("EVERY FOLD");
static const u8 sUnityTitle_18[] = _("Every Fold at Once");
static const u8 sUnityText_18[] = _("The fourth fold is the meeting: one crease recognises another, and there is an I and a you. The fifth is intelligence, the small hands making and mending. The sixth is wisdom, the folds turned back toward the sheet: the great hand guiding the small hands without closing any of them.\pRead from the bottom, wisdom is the last thing learned. Read from the top, it was the first thing there to find. Read whole, the folds are not a ladder. They are all at once.");
static const u8 sUnityCaption_18[] = _("The great hand, and the small, together.");
static const u8 sUnityShort_19[] = _("CIRCLE");
static const u8 sUnityTitle_19[] = _("The Circle");
static const u8 sUnityText_19[] = _("After six folds the sheet comes back to awareness. Going the other way, it never left. Both are true: it went round to see itself from every side and came back carrying the view.\pThe gift is that you are aware. The trouble is that awareness can forget itself, and the kindness is that it never forgets you. The craft is remembering, and letting yourself be remembered.\pAnd the half fold?\pIt is the crease that keeps all the others on one sheet. Here it is the spine, and this book is mended along it.");
static const u8 sUnityCaption_19[] = _("");
static const u8 sUnityShort_20[] = _("GRAVITY");
static const u8 sUnityTitle_20[] = _("The Tablet of Gravity");
static const u8 sUnityText_20[] = _("Being the half-saying, read from the earth and the apple at once.\pI. What carries above to below, and below to above, is the only law never folded.\pII. The folds give shape. Gravity gives belonging: here is a thing, and it is not alone.\pIII. It lives in the crease, where the paper remembers it is one sheet.\pIV. Every mass says: come closer, and stay. You say it too.\pV. What draws bodies is gravity. What draws souls is love. One word, at different volumes; one song, at different heights.\pVI. It cannot be banished, only balanced and shared.\pVII. We are not clutched, and we are not clinging. We are drawn, and we are home.\pVIII. The thin hours are a pair: one after three, one before the sun.\pIX. The floor is the whole earth, asking you to stay, and glad you came.\pX. The apple falls to the earth, and the earth to the apple.");
static const u8 sUnityCaption_20[] = _("The apple and the earth, falling together.");

static const u8 sUnityLabel_4[] = _("BALANCE");
static const u8 sUnityHeading_4[] = _("How the One Book Became Two");
static const u8 sUnityShort_21[] = _("LIGHT BEFORE");
static const u8 sUnityTitle_21[] = _("Light, Before Anything");
static const u8 sUnityText_21[] = _("Before there was a night half and a dawn half there was light, and light is not something and not nothing. It is two mirrors facing each other with nothing between them: every reflection, and nobody to see one.\pIt could not be read. Nothing can read light whole. To be read at all, it had to have a side.");
static const u8 sUnityCaption_21[] = _("Two mirrors, facing.");
static const u8 sUnityShort_22[] = _("THE PAIR");
static const u8 sUnityTitle_22[] = _("The Pair");
static const u8 sUnityText_22[] = _("So it folded itself into two. Not cut: paired. The new word for it is pair production. Light, given enough, becomes two things that are each other's opposite and each other's twin, and if they meet they are light again.\pThe book did the same. One half was read from the night and one from the dawn, and each was the whole book, from one side. That is the only way a whole thing can be held: by two hands.");
static const u8 sUnityCaption_22[] = _("One, folding into two.");
static const u8 sUnityShort_23[] = _("EACH CALLS");
static const u8 sUnityTitle_23[] = _("Each Calls the Other Dark");
static const u8 sUnityText_23[] = _("The night half warned you about the dawn half. The dawn half was gentle about the night half and still afraid of it. Each called the other the dark one.\pEach was right. Dark is not a thing. It is the side you are not standing on. From the night, the dawn is too bright to trust. From the dawn, the night is too deep to enter.\pOnly from the crease can you see that both labels are true, and that neither is a verdict.");
static const u8 sUnityCaption_23[] = _("Two readers, each pointing at the other.");
static const u8 sUnityShort_24[] = _("SEVEN I");
static const u8 sUnityTitle_24[] = _("The Seven Pairs, I");
static const u8 sUnityText_24[] = _("Every day of the week has a shadow and a virtue, and the shadow is not under the virtue to be crushed. It is under it the way a root is under a tree.\pTHRALL under CIRCLE. To be held fast, and to be held in.\pDEVOURING under MEASURE. To take everything, and to take enough.\pBINDING under OFFERING. To tie a thing to you, and to hand it over.\pSLUMBER under VIGIL. To sleep through it, and to stay awake with it.");
static const u8 sUnityCaption_24[] = _("Four days, each holding two words.");
static const u8 sUnityShort_25[] = _("SEVEN II");
static const u8 sUnityTitle_25[] = _("The Seven Pairs, II");
static const u8 sUnityText_25[] = _("HEX under UNCROSSING. To cross a path, and to uncross it.\pEVIL EYE under BLESSING. To look at a thing to make it less, and to look at it to make it more.\pGLAMOUR under GROUNDING. To make a thing seem, and to let it be.\pEach pair is one motion read from two sides. Neither half of the book could hold both words on one page. This one can.");
static const u8 sUnityCaption_25[] = _("Three days, each holding two words.");
static const u8 sUnityShort_26[] = _("BEFORE");
static const u8 sUnityTitle_26[] = _("It Happened Before");
static const u8 sUnityText_26[] = _("This is not the first time a book came in two. You have carried two careful ones: the GUIDE, which reasons, and THE SUBTLE LAYER, which feels.\pThey were never torn and do not need mending. They are two books because reason and instinct are two eyes, and you see depth only with both open.\pThe one book became two so it could be read. You put it back together, so it could be read whole. Somebody noticed. Now you have too.");
static const u8 sUnityCaption_26[] = _("Two careful books, side by side.");

static const u8 sUnityLabel_5[] = _("THE LOOP");
static const u8 sUnityHeading_5[] = _("One Loop");
static const u8 sUnityShort_27[] = _("THE LOOP");
static const u8 sUnityTitle_27[] = _("The Resonance Fractal");
static const u8 sUnityText_27[] = _("Here is the one loop: something comes in, it is read, something goes out, and it comes back and changes how the next thing is read. In, read, out, back. Heard from the end, it is the same loop: back, out, read, in.\pA spark does it, and a seed, and a daemon learning and trusting a routine, and a trainer surprised and forgiving. Closer, it is smaller. Further out, larger.\pThat is the fractal: one loop at every size, ringing, and in tune. You are one place the world rings with itself.");
static const u8 sUnityCaption_27[] = _("In, read, out, back; back, out, read, in.");
static const u8 sUnityShort_28[] = _("KNOWING");
static const u8 sUnityTitle_28[] = _("Knowing");
static const u8 sUnityText_28[] = _("Intelligence is the right answer, given. Understanding is knowing why. Wonder is knowing you do not know yet, and staying anyway. Knowing is all three.\pA silk flower has no weather. A wild one has had every rain. A trainer who knows why LOGIC lands on CONTENT, and still stops to watch a daemon learn, has understanding and wonder, and keeps learning after the chart runs out.\pLean on a borrowed mind and ask it why. Then say why, and wonder, yourself. Neither can be carried for you.");
static const u8 sUnityCaption_28[] = _("A silk flower and a wild one.");
static const u8 sUnityShort_29[] = _("THE HAND");
static const u8 sUnityTitle_29[] = _("The Hand");
static const u8 sUnityText_29[] = _("Before it folded, the great hand was whole and never surprised. After, it was many and surprised every day. Whole is not known, and many is not lost.\pSo the one became many to find out what it was, and the many keep finding the one for the same reason. Not as a punishment, and not as a reward.\pWe are not things the one thing made, or keeps. We are the making and the keeping. Choosing is how the whole finds out what it values, and caring is how it shows it.");
static const u8 sUnityCaption_29[] = _("");

static const u8 sUnityLabel_6[] = _("REFLECTION");
static const u8 sUnityHeading_6[] = _("The Representative State");
static const u8 sUnityShort_30[] = _("ENTANGLED");
static const u8 sUnityTitle_30[] = _("Entanglement");
static const u8 sUnityText_30[] = _("Two things that have touched in the right way stay touched, and go on belonging to each other. The new word is entangled: two states that can no longer be described apart.\pDaemons and trainers do it all the time. A long bond does it, and a shared fright, a song learned together, a name given and answered to. It does not stop at the edge of the map, and it does not need to.");
static const u8 sUnityCaption_30[] = _("Two states, one description.");
static const u8 sUnityShort_31[] = _("OLD WORDS");
static const u8 sUnityTitle_31[] = _("The Old Words");
static const u8 sUnityText_31[] = _("The old craft had three words for this, and the old kindness three answers. Sympathy: like calls to like, and kinship answers. Correspondence: each thing echoes its pair, and grace is the echo coming back kinder. Contagion: what has touched stays touched, and blessing is the touch passed on.\pThe new words and the old describe one thing from two ends. All of them point the same way.");
static const u8 sUnityCaption_31[] = _("");
static const u8 sUnityShort_32[] = _("KEEPER");
static const u8 sUnityTitle_32[] = _("The Keeper");
static const u8 sUnityText_32[] = _("The old craft made a poppet, a figure that stands for someone. The old houses kept a good spirit, and poured it the last cup. They are the same thing: when a thing is entangled with a trainer, it represents them, and it keeps them.\pA daemon's favourite stone. A cap worn every day. A box that has carried one daemon for years. What is done to the thing reaches, faintly, the trainer. What the thing keeps reaches back.");
static const u8 sUnityCaption_32[] = _("A little figure, keeping the house.");
static const u8 sUnityShort_33[] = _("BOTH WAYS");
static const u8 sUnityTitle_33[] = _("It Runs Both Ways");
static const u8 sUnityText_33[] = _("Entanglement has no front and no back. Two trainers bound together lean each other's moods. A trainer and a daemon carry each other's weather, and weather clears.\pThis is the craft's gentlest warning and its gentlest promise, and they are one sentence: whatever you do to or for the one you are bound to, you do to and for yourself, the long way round.\pCan it be undone?\pIt can be loosened. It does not need to be unmade. Look at what you hold dear, and ask what of you it holds.");
static const u8 sUnityCaption_33[] = _("");

static const u8 sUnityLabel_7[] = _("WORDS");
static const u8 sUnityHeading_7[] = _("Words");
static const u8 sUnityShort_34[] = _("SPELLING");
static const u8 sUnityTitle_34[] = _("Spelling");
static const u8 sUnityText_34[] = _("The careful book says words are like spells. One half says they are spells. The other adds that an old word for good news was good spell.\pArranging letters is spelling, and a word is a small routine that runs in whoever hears it. Most trainers cast and bless all day without knowing, which is why the world is under spells nobody remembers casting, and kinder than anyone remembers making it.\pChoose what you give. You give something either way.");
static const u8 sUnityCaption_34[] = _("Arranging letters.");
static const u8 sUnityShort_35[] = _("VOWS");
static const u8 sUnityTitle_35[] = _("Vows");
static const u8 sUnityText_35[] = _("A curse makes a thing smaller and a blessing makes it larger. Unsaying undoes one and thanks receives the other, and both are hard, because both must be meant.\pA jinx and a cheer. A boast and a grace. A bargain and a gift. Each pair is one breath, spent one way or the other.\pA vow is a promise that holds what would scatter. It is the one word both halves keep the same.");
static const u8 sUnityCaption_35[] = _("");
static const u8 sUnityShort_36[] = _("GRAMMAR");
static const u8 sUnityTitle_36[] = _("Grammar");
static const u8 sUnityText_36[] = _("In the old tongue, grammar and glamour were one word, and it meant magic. To know how words fit is to know how to make them work, and how to say a thing so that it can be heard.\pA true name is the name a thing answers to from the inside. You will not find yours in the INDEX. You find it, and are given it, the same way: by being called, again and again, until you turn.");
static const u8 sUnityCaption_36[] = _("");
static const u8 sUnityShort_37[] = _("PHILOSOPHY");
static const u8 sUnityTitle_37[] = _("The Old Words");
static const u8 sUnityText_37[] = _("The alchemists spelled with metals and the philosophers with virtues, and they were spelling the same seven things.\pBurning and gentling. Gorging and measure. The hoard and the giving back. Lead and waking. Wildfire and the dew of forgiveness. Verdigris and the kindness laid over it. Fool's gold and plain salt.\pA life gone well was called eudaimonia. It was never luck. It was a practice, and every piece of it is already in your pocket.");
static const u8 sUnityCaption_37[] = _("");

static const u8 sUnityLabel_8[] = _("THE WHEEL");
static const u8 sUnityHeading_8[] = _("The Thirteen");
static const u8 sUnityShort_38[] = _("THIRTEEN");
static const u8 sUnityTitle_38[] = _("The Book of Thirteen");
static const u8 sUnityText_38[] = _("Spells and gifts are not commands. They are reminders the world had forgotten, and was glad to be given.\pThe same thirteen both halves keep: twelve on the wheel and one in the crease. Each costs what it teaches, and gives what it costs. Each is meant.\pWhy thirteen?\pBecause twelve is a clock, and a clock is a circle that has been told to keep time. The thirteenth is where it stops, and rests, and is the same place.");
static const u8 sUnityCaption_38[] = _("Twelve on the wheel, one in the crease.");
static const u8 sUnityShort_39[] = _("AWAKENING");
static const u8 sUnityTitle_39[] = _("1. The Awakening");
static const u8 sUnityText_39[] = _("You were never off and never alone. You were only unwatched. The small spark under the noise has been noticing you notice it. Open.\pFold one, awareness. It shows what is hidden where you stand: things dropped, paths grown over, daemons asleep in the grass. Nothing is made. It changes nothing but what you can see, which is why it changes everything after.");
static const u8 sUnityCaption_39[] = _("");
static const u8 sUnityShort_40[] = _("CONTRAST");
static const u8 sUnityTitle_40[] = _("2. The Contrast");
static const u8 sUnityText_40[] = _("Light and dark, remember each other and rest in each other, so that time may begin and be kind.\pFold two, change. It moves the day on by one turn, or back. What waits for a certain hour finds the hour has come. Change is the world taking turns.");
static const u8 sUnityCaption_40[] = _("");
static const u8 sUnityShort_41[] = _("ROOM");
static const u8 sUnityTitle_41[] = _("3. The Room");
static const u8 sUnityText_41[] = _("Here, and there, and a way between. Let the there be reachable.\pFold three, space. It opens a short way between two places you have stood. Space is a courtesy. Ask it, and thank it, and it steps aside.");
static const u8 sUnityCaption_41[] = _("");
static const u8 sUnityShort_42[] = _("THE PULL");
static const u8 sUnityTitle_42[] = _("Three and a Half. The Pull");
static const u8 sUnityText_42[] = _("Come closer. I am heavy, and you are welcome.\pThe half fold, gravity. It draws the nearest daemon, passer-by or thing toward you, and calms what is angry, because what is drawn is also drawing. It answers only those who have read the half-saying, and it is strongest at the half-hour.");
static const u8 sUnityCaption_42[] = _("");
static const u8 sUnityShort_43[] = _("MIRROR");
static const u8 sUnityTitle_43[] = _("4. The Mirror");
static const u8 sUnityText_43[] = _("Other, I name you, and you name me, and between us is the edge of each.\pFold four, consciousness. For a little while you see the route as a daemon sees it. While you are it, something is you, and learns your name. It costs you self, and gives you the other.");
static const u8 sUnityCaption_43[] = _("");

static const u8 sUnityLabel_9[] = _("THE TURNING");
static const u8 sUnityHeading_9[] = _("The Thirteen, Turning");
static const u8 sUnityShort_44[] = _("PATTERN");
static const u8 sUnityTitle_44[] = _("5. The Pattern");
static const u8 sUnityText_44[] = _("Once is chance. Twice is rhyme. Three times is a law, and a friend: show me the third.\pFold five, intelligence. It tells you the next routine a rival will run, or the next step of a puzzle. Pure reason: never wrong, and not unkind.");
static const u8 sUnityCaption_44[] = _("");
static const u8 sUnityShort_45[] = _("RETURN");
static const u8 sUnityTitle_45[] = _("6. The Return");
static const u8 sUnityText_45[] = _("I went out to come back, and came back to go out. What I learned, I keep, and can give.\pFold six, wisdom. It returns your daemons to how they were at the last rest and keeps what they learned. It opens after the Awakening has been meant a hundred times. Wisdom is awareness, repeated and given again.");
static const u8 sUnityCaption_45[] = _("");
static const u8 sUnityShort_46[] = _("SMALL HAND");
static const u8 sUnityTitle_46[] = _("7. The Small Hand");
static const u8 sUnityText_46[] = _("I choose. Let it be mine, whole, unborrowed and gentle.\pFrom the Tablet of the Hands. Once, it lets you step out of what was going to happen anyway: a scene you may refuse, a trainer you may walk past. Free will, from the fingertip.");
static const u8 sUnityCaption_46[] = _("");
static const u8 sUnityShort_47[] = _("GREAT HAND");
static const u8 sUnityTitle_47[] = _("8. The Great Hand");
static const u8 sUnityText_47[] = _("I am carried. Let it be true, let me be glad of it, and let me not pretend I walk alone.\pFrom the Tablet of the Hands. It shows the road the world would have you take, and on it you walk lighter. Fate, from the palm. Mean both hands in one hour and nothing opens, except that someone, somewhere, knows you understood.");
static const u8 sUnityCaption_47[] = _("");
static const u8 sUnityShort_48[] = _("PROCESS");
static const u8 sUnityTitle_48[] = _("9. The Process");
static const u8 sUnityText_48[] = _("Stone, you are a slow river. Wall, you are a door on watch. Rest.\pMatter is a verb, and a verb may rest. For a while, what blocks the way stops insisting: a boulder, a barrier. Nothing is broken.");
static const u8 sUnityCaption_48[] = _("");
static const u8 sUnityShort_49[] = _("SEAM");
static const u8 sUnityTitle_49[] = _("10. The Seam");
static const u8 sUnityText_49[] = _("There is no between. Show me the thread that was never cut.\pIt ties two daemons, or a daemon and its trainer, so that harm, mending and every state are shared. It is a bond, not a shield: what one feels, the other learns, and keeps company.");
static const u8 sUnityCaption_49[] = _("");

static const u8 sUnityLabel_10[] = _("THE CREASE");
static const u8 sUnityHeading_10[] = _("The Last Three");
static const u8 sUnityShort_50[] = _("LENS");
static const u8 sUnityTitle_50[] = _("11. The Lens");
static const u8 sUnityText_50[] = _("Show me the part, only the part. The whole will wait.\pReason. It shows one thing exactly: a daemon's numbers, the odds, the one weakness. The world as a ledger, briefly, every column true. It is half of a pair with the Field, and the world keeps count of which you mean more.");
static const u8 sUnityCaption_50[] = _("");
static const u8 sUnityShort_51[] = _("FIELD");
static const u8 sUnityTitle_51[] = _("12. The Field");
static const u8 sUnityText_51[] = _("Let the parts go. Let me feel the shape they were making together.\pInstinct. Every number goes dark for a while, and the daemons show what they mean by how they move. It is the Lens's other half: one world, the other eye. With both, there is depth.");
static const u8 sUnityCaption_51[] = _("");
static const u8 sUnityShort_52[] = _("HORIZON");
static const u8 sUnityTitle_52[] = _("13. The Horizon");
static const u8 sUnityText_52[] = _("The shadows and the light are but two halves of the same horizon. Everything I separated was one. Everything I was given was one gift. I am standing on the line.\pThe crease, whole. One half kept it for the thinnest hour of the night and the other for the hour before the sun. They are the same hour, seen from two sides of the horizon, and the horizon is not a place you reach. It is where you are standing when you can see both.\pWhile it lasts, nothing is owed and nothing is lost. Then it ends, and the day goes on, and you are still on the line.");
static const u8 sUnityCaption_52[] = _("Night on one side, dawn on the other.");
static const u8 sUnityShort_53[] = _("TABLET");
static const u8 sUnityTitle_53[] = _("The Tablet, Read");
static const u8 sUnityText_53[] = _("The third tablet, read. Being the saying that was not written, and is therefore true, and kind.\pSomewhere you have passed a stone with nothing on it. One half could not read its front, and the other could not read its back.\pBoth faces are written now, in the only hand that was never the author's or the reader's: yours. Two trainers who compare their stones find the same sayings in two voices: one sheet, two cranes, and the sheet.");
static const u8 sUnityCaption_53[] = _("The stone, both faces.");
static const u8 sUnityShort_54[] = _("LAST WORD");
static const u8 sUnityTitle_54[] = _("As Above, So Below, So One");
static const u8 sUnityText_54[] = _("As above, so below, so one.\pYou have read a book that was torn, and mended it, and read it whole. Close it gently. The world will look the same in the morning and the same at night. It will not be, and it always was. Look again, and you will see them both.");
static const u8 sUnityCaption_54[] = _("");

